Since \( \triangle ABC \) is isosceles with \( AB = AC \), the base angles \( \angle B \) and \( \angle C \) are equal. Therefore, we have:
\[ \angle B = \angle C \]
\[ 2x = 4y - 5 \]

The sum of the angles in a triangle is \( 180^\circ \):
\[ \angle A + \angle B + \angle C = 180^\circ \]
