Next, calculate \( 2\pi (49)(80) \):

\[ 2\pi (49)(80) = 2\pi \times 3920 = 7840\pi \]

Now, add these two results together:

\[ \text{Surface Area} = 4802\pi + 7840\pi = 12642\pi \]

Finally, approximate \( \pi \) as 3.14159 to find the numerical value:

