 To find the volume of a sphere, we use the formula:

\[ V = \frac{4}{3} \pi r^3 \]

where \( r \) is the radius of the sphere.

From the image, the diameter of the sphere is given as 22.36 mm. The radius \( r \) is half of the diameter:

\[ r = \frac{22.36}{2} = 11.18 \text{ mm} \]

Now, substitute the radius into the volume formula:

\[ V = \frac{4}{3} \pi (11.18)^3 \]

First, calculate \( (11.18)^3 \):

\[ (11.18)^3 = 11.18 \times 11.18 \times 11.18 \approx 1390.07 \]

Now, substitute this value back into the volume formula:

\[ V = \frac{4}{3} \pi \times 1390.07 \]

Using \( \pi \approx 3.14159 \):

\[ V \approx \frac{4}{3} \times 3.14159 \times 1390.07 \]
\[ V \approx 4.18879 \times 1390.07 \]
\[ V \approx 5807.48 \]

So, the volume of the sphere is approximately 5807.48 cubic millimeters, correct to two decimal places.

Answer: \boxed{5807.48}
