   \]
   where \( b_1 \) and \( b_2 \) are the lengths of the two parallel sides, and \( h \) is the height.

   Here, \( b_1 = 18 \) cm, \( b_2 = 10 \) cm, and \( h = 3 \) cm.
   \[
   \text{Area} = \frac{1}{2} \times (18 + 10) \times 3 = \frac{1}{2} \times 28 \times 3 = 42 \text{ cm}^2
   \]

